// Gap 4: the `move closure(i32)` parameter expands to three C arguments at the
// native call, so `kelp_call_twice(thunk, env, destroy, x)` matches the
// helper's `(fn, data, destroy, x)` prototype. The closure's own signature
// must be all by-value scalars, and the parameter is `move` because the native
// side takes ownership (its `destroy` notify is the only thing that frees the
// environment).
pub extern fun kelp_call_twice(f: move closure(i32), x: i32).return: i32
